# Generated from: specs/18-create-a-durable-accountless-volunteer-action-hub/requirements.md
Feature: Create a durable accountless volunteer action hub
  As a volunteer
  I want one private link that remains useful through my commitment
  So that I can see status and take currently valid actions without an account or repeated coordinator intervention

  @SCN001
  Scenario: One request capability follows the commitment lifecycle
    Given a future request has one valid private status capability
    When a coordinator approves it
    Then the same link displays complete local commitment context and Assigned status
    And offers Confirm and Decline before shift start
    When the volunteer confirms
    Then the same link displays Confirmed status and offers Cancel before shift end
    And replay of confirmation changes nothing

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Access lifetime follows the commitment rather than a fixed issue date
    Given a valid hub was issued more than 30 days before its shift
    When it is used before or at seven days after the current shift end
    Then read-only status remains available
    And an authorized shift date correction changes the access deadline without rewriting the token
    When the grace deadline passes
    Then the same link is uniformly invalid and changes nothing

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Recovery does not enumerate or invalidate current access
    Given matching and nonmatching email plus local commitment date submissions
    When an anonymous caller submits each recovery form
    Then both receive the same generic receipt
    And matching commitments enqueue at most three separately scoped recovery deliveries
    And no current hub is invalidated by request, send, or delivery failure

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Recovery redemption atomically replaces access
    Given a matching volunteer receives a 30-minute single-use recovery token
    And an old hub remains valid
    When the recovery token is redeemed
    Then it is consumed once
    And all old hubs for that volunteer and slot are invalidated
    And one new raw hub capability is returned while only its hash persists
    And concurrent or replayed redemption changes nothing

  @SCN005
  Scenario Outline: Coordinator manages failed or compromised access
    Given coverage reports the volunteer access as <state>
    When the coordinator chooses <operation> and confirms its consequences
    Then replacement delivery state remains visible and the actor/mode are audited
    And current access is <old_access>

    Examples:
      | state            | operation                     | old_access                         |
      | Message not sent | Send replacement access       | valid until recovery redemption    |
      | Active           | Revoke now and send replacement| invalid immediately                |

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Previously issued action links drain without extension
    Given a separate assignment action link was issued before hub cutover
    When it is used before its stored expiry and action deadline
    Then the existing single-use transition may succeed
    When it is replayed or used after stored expiry
    Then it is uniformly invalid and changes nothing
    And no application path creates or extends a legacy action token after cutover
